title: barbarian_relic
---
Narrator:
At the center of the ritual site, your salvage crew finds it.

---

Narrator:
It is not large. It is roughly the size and shape of a navigation sphere, but it is not a navigation sphere.

It has no seams. No visible power source. It is warm to the touch and has been warm for longer than anyone wants to calculate.

---

Narrator:
The hordes did not build this.

The hordes found this, long ago, and they have been worshipping it ever since.

---

Narrator:
Your science officer says she can interface with it. She says this with the kind of certainty that means she already has.

She is very calm when she says this. That is the most alarming part.

---

-> [Integrate the relic into fleet systems]
    <<apply_effect "relic_empowerment">>
    Narrator:
    The process takes six hours. Your engineer supervises without asking questions.

    Narrator:
    Afterwards, the fleet's attack systems register improved targeting coherence.

    Narrator:
    Your science officer does not speak for the rest of the day.

    Narrator:
    You do not ask her what she saw.

-> [Destroy the relic]
    <<apply_effect "horde_tribute">>
    Narrator:
    The shaped charge is small. The effect is not.

    Narrator:
    The relic comes apart without sound. The pieces do not look like pieces of anything that was once whole.

    Narrator:
    Three days later, the horde activity in the surrounding systems drops sharply.

    Narrator:
    You don't know whether you helped or unleashed something worse.

    Narrator:
    Fleet command thanks you for securing the system.

    Narrator:
    You do not mention the relic in your report.

===
